**Vulkan: `GGML_ASSERT(wg0 <= maxComputeWorkGroupCount[0] ...)` crash on prompts past ~64K tokens — `ggml_vk_fill`/`ggml_vk_arange` dispatch flat 1D grids**

Hit while testing this PR at 035e227 on Vulkan (3× Intel Arc Pro B70, layer split, `-c 131072 -fa on`, unsloth UD-Q3_K_XL): any prompt whose prefill crosses ~64K tokens aborts:

```
ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp:8168: GGML_ASSERT(wg0 <= ctx->device->properties.limits.maxComputeWorkGroupCount[0] && ...) failed
```

Adding a print of the pipeline name at the assert site identified the op:

```
pipeline=fill_f16 wg=(65792,1,1) limits=(65536,65536,65536) elements=(33685504,1,1)
```

`ggml_vk_fill` dispatches `{ggml_nelements(dst), 1, 1}` flat. One of the qwen4exp context-scaled buffers reaches 33.7M elements around n_past ≈ 64K, i.e. 65,792 workgroups of 512 in x — over Intel's 65,536-per-dimension `maxComputeWorkGroupCount`. Reproducible at the same boundary regardless of ubatch: a 57.7K-token prompt completes, 66.5K crashes mid-prefill. `ggml_vk_arange` has the same pattern (not yet observed to trigger, but the same overflow is reachable).

The fill/arange dispatch code is mainline rather than introduced here, but this model seems to be the first to size a filled buffer past the limit, so posting where the affected users are.

Fix that works for me — fold the 1D grid into 2D on the host and linearize the invocation id in the shaders (both already bounds-check `i >= p.KX`, so the padded tail is harmless):

```diff
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
@@ ggml_vk_add1 (after) @@
+// Fold a flat element-wise dispatch into 2D when x alone would exceed the
+// device's maxComputeWorkGroupCount (Intel Vulkan: 65536). Safe for
+// order-free element-wise ops whose shader linearizes gl_GlobalInvocationID
+// as y * (gl_NumWorkGroups.x * wgsize) + x and bounds-checks against KX
+// (fill.comp, arange.comp do).
+static std::array<uint32_t, 3> ggml_vk_fold_1d_elements(ggml_backend_vk_context * ctx, const vk_pipeline &pipeline, uint32_t ne) {
+    const uint32_t wgsz    = pipeline->wg_denoms[0];
+    const uint32_t max_wg0 = ctx->device->properties.limits.maxComputeWorkGroupCount[0];
+    uint32_t nx = ne, ny = 1;
+    if (CEIL_DIV(ne, wgsz) > max_wg0) {
+        const uint32_t total_wg = CEIL_DIV(ne, wgsz);
+        ny = CEIL_DIV(total_wg, max_wg0);
+        nx = CEIL_DIV(total_wg, ny) * wgsz;
+    }
+    return { nx, ny, 1 };
+}
@@ ggml_vk_arange @@
-    std::array<uint32_t, 3> elements = { (uint32_t)ggml_nelements(dst), 1, 1 };
+    const std::array<uint32_t, 3> elements = ggml_vk_fold_1d_elements(ctx, pipeline, (uint32_t)ggml_nelements(dst));
@@ ggml_vk_fill @@
-    std::array<uint32_t, 3> elements = { (uint32_t)ggml_nelements(dst), 1, 1 };
+    const std::array<uint32_t, 3> elements = ggml_vk_fold_1d_elements(ctx, pipeline, (uint32_t)ggml_nelements(dst));
```

```diff
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/fill.comp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/fill.comp
@@
-    const uint i = gl_GlobalInvocationID.x;
+    // Host may split oversized 1D grids across y; plain dispatches have y == 0
+    // and this reduces to the old expression.
+    const uint i = gl_GlobalInvocationID.y * (gl_NumWorkGroups.x * gl_WorkGroupSize.x) + gl_GlobalInvocationID.x;
```

```diff
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/arange.comp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/arange.comp
@@
-    const uint i = gl_GlobalInvocationID.x;
+    // Same 2D fold as fill.comp.
+    const uint i = gl_GlobalInvocationID.y * (gl_NumWorkGroups.x * gl_WorkGroupSize.x) + gl_GlobalInvocationID.x;
```

Validated after the fix: a 66,585-token needle-in-haystack prompt prefills and retrieves correctly on the same hardware (previously crashed at the same size). Happy to open this against mainline instead if that's the better home for it.

build_attn_qsa 对量化 KV 缓存（--cache-type-k q8_0）缺 Hadamard 旋转处理，会在 qwen4exp.cpp:544 断言崩溃；本 patch 对齐了标准 build_attn 的旋转/反旋转逻辑

```
# xzz @ DESKTOP-BR61NP5 in ~/son [7:45:34] C:130
$ cat ~/son/qwen4exp-attn-rot-fix.patch
diff --git a/src/models/qwen4exp.cpp b/src/models/qwen4exp.cpp
index 65e9b1991..c384a17ad 100644
--- a/src/models/qwen4exp.cpp
+++ b/src/models/qwen4exp.cpp
@@ -541,7 +541,15 @@ ggml_tensor * llama_model_qwen4exp::graph::build_attn_qsa(
         ggml_tensor *             top_k,
         float                     kq_scale,
         int                       il) {
-    GGML_ASSERT(inp->self_k_rot == nullptr && inp->self_v_rot == nullptr);
+    // apply Hadamard rotation for quantized KV cache, matching build_attn
+    if (inp->self_k_rot) {
+        q_cur = llama_mul_mat_hadamard(ctx0, q_cur, inp->self_k_rot);
+        k_cur = llama_mul_mat_hadamard(ctx0, k_cur, inp->self_k_rot);
+    }
+
+    if (inp->self_v_rot) {
+        v_cur = llama_mul_mat_hadamard(ctx0, v_cur, inp->self_v_rot);
+    }

     // these nodes are added to the graph together so that they are not reordered
     // by doing so, the number of splits in the graph is reduced
@@ -596,6 +604,10 @@ ggml_tensor * llama_model_qwen4exp::graph::build_attn_qsa(
     ggml_tensor * cur = build_attn_mha(q, k, v, nullptr, kq_mask_top_k, nullptr, nullptr, kq_scale, il);
     cb(cur, "kqv_out", il);

+    if (inp->self_v_rot) {
+        cur = llama_mul_mat_hadamard(ctx0, cur, inp->self_v_rot);
+    }
+
     return cur;
 }
```
